# Kiro Hyprland editions: folders open in Thunar.
# Without a default, Disk Usage Analyzer (baobab, also on the ISO) won: it comes first alphabetically
# among the apps that declare inode/directory. Read only in Hyprland sessions (XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=Hyprland);
# a user's own ~/.config/mimeapps.list (e.g. set by Kirotux Hyprland Premium's Default apps) still wins.
[Default Applications]
inode/directory=thunar.desktop
